<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (STATIONNAME column in the dataset refers to the different meteorological and agricultural data collection stations across Tunisia. These stations are distributed throughout the country, representing various regions with distinct climatic conditions, such as coastal, inland, and desert zones. Each station is positioned in a specific geographical location, providing valuable insights into regional variations in climate, soil conditions, and agricultural practices. By analyzing the distribution of stations, we can observe how different areas of Tunisia contribute to the dataset, with each station offering data relevant to the crops grown and the environmental factors influencing agricultural productivity. For instance, stations located in coastal regions might experience more temperate climates, while those in inland or desert areas could be characterized by harsher, arid conditions. Understanding the geographical spread of these stations is crucial for assessing regional agricultural yield, maturity times, and other related factors, as the local climate plays a significant role in crop growth. This distribution also allows for targeted recommendations and predictions based on specific regional needs and challenges, thereby aiding in more precise agricultural planning and management.)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [2]
>>
