/E (The provided visualizations illustrate the distribution of agricultural stations in Tunisia by irrigation type. The bar chart on the left shows the number of stations for each governorate, separated into irrigated \(orange\) and rainfed \(blue\) categories. It is evident that in most regions, irrigated stations outnumber rainfed ones, with particularly high counts observed in governorates such as Sousse, Sidi Bouzid, and Kairouan. The donut chart on the right complements this by presenting the proportional distribution of stations by governorate and irrigation type. Each segment represents a governorate, with the inner ring reflecting rainfed stations and the outer ring showing irrigated stations. The percentages indicate that the distribution is relatively balanced across regions, with most governorates contributing between 6% and 6.5% of the total stations, regardless of irrigation type. This detailed breakdown highlights both the regional concentration and the overall parity in the deployment of irrigation methods across Tunisia.)
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [1 2]
