1302 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/T (THE DATASET WAS SUBSEQUENTLY DIVIDED INTO TRAINING AND TESTING SETS, EMPLOYING AN 80/20 SPLIT. THIS DIVISION IS CRITICAL FOR EVALUATING THE MODEL'S PERFORMANCE ON UNSEEN DATA, ENSURING THAT THE MODEL CAN GENERALIZE EFFECTIVELY. THE FEATURE SET \(X\) WAS CONSTRUCTED BY EXCLUDING THE TARGET VARIABLE, YIELD \(YA\), AND ANY OTHER IDENTIFIERS TO PREVENT DATA LEAKAGE. THE CORRESPONDING TARGET VARIABLE \(Y\) CONTAINED ONLY THE YIELD VALUES THAT WERE TO BE PREDICTED. ADDITIONALLY, THE ORDER OF FEATURES UTILIZED IN TRAINING WAS METICULOUSLY RECORDED, ENSURING CONSISTENCY FOR FUTURE MODELING STEPS AND DEPLOYMENT. THIS STRUCTURED APPROACH TO DATA PREPARATION IS VITAL FOR MAINTAINING THE INTEGRITY AND REPRODUCIBILITY OF THE MODELING PROCESS.)
