/Pg 92 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
1818 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (MobileNetV2 was chosen for this project due to its lightweight architecture and efficiency in handling complex image classification tasks while being computationally efficient. This is particularly important when working with large datasets of plant disease images, as it allows for faster processing and deployment, especially on devices with limited computational resources. )
/Pg 92 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1819 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (MobileNetV2's inverted residual structure and depthwise separable convolutions help retain high accuracy while minimizing the number of parameters, making it ideal for real-time applications in agriculture. Its ability to generalize well across different tasks, such as object recognition, makes it a suitable choice for detecting various plant diseases with robust performance.)
/Pg 92 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
