1902 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/T (The goal of this phase is to classify volunteer plants into one of three categories: harmful weed, useful weed, or medicinal plant. While the model predicts the species of the plant, the ultimate objective is to categorize the plant based on its potential usefulness or harmfulness. This classification is determined by referencing a CSV file, mentioned earlier in the data acquisition phase, which associates each plant species with its respective category. Given the similarity in appearance between these plants, selecting the right model architecture was crucial. I chose the Xception model for its proven effectiveness in image classification, particularly for fine-grained categories like plant species. This section outlines the process of model building, training and evaluation , highlighting how each step was tailored to meet the specific requirements of the Xception model for this task.)
/E (The goal of this phase is to classify volunteer plants into one of three categories: harmful weed, useful weed, or medicinal plant. While the model predicts the species of the plant, the ultimate objective is to categorize the plant based on its potential usefulness or harmfulness. This classification is determined by referencing a CSV file, mentioned earlier in the data acquisition phase, which associates each plant species with its respective category. Given the similarity in appearance between these plants, selecting the right model architecture was crucial. I chose the Xception model for its proven effectiveness in image classification, particularly for fine-grained categories like plant species. This section outlines the process of model building, training and evaluation , highlighting how each step was tailored to meet the specific requirements of the Xception model for this task.)
/Pg 100 0 R
/K [3]
