2327 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/T (THE IMAGE WAS RESIZED TO THE TARGET SIZE OF 299X299 PIXELS, WHICH IS THE INPUT SIZE EXPECTED BY THE XCEPTION MODEL. IT WAS THEN CONVERTED INTO A NUMPY ARRAY, EXPANDED TO MATCH THE MODEL'S EXPECTED INPUT SHAPE, AND NORMALIZED BY SCALING PIXEL VALUES TO THE RANGE [0, 1]. THE PREPROCESSED IMAGE WAS PASSED TO THE TRAINED XCEPTION MODEL FOR PREDICTION. THE MODEL RETURNED A SET OF CLASS PROBABILITIES, AND THE CLASS WITH THE HIGHEST PROBABILITY WAS CHOSEN AS THE PREDICTED LABEL.)
/E (THE IMAGE WAS RESIZED TO THE TARGET SIZE OF 299X299 PIXELS, WHICH IS THE INPUT SIZE EXPECTED BY THE XCEPTION MODEL. IT WAS THEN CONVERTED INTO A NUMPY ARRAY, EXPANDED TO MATCH THE MODEL'S EXPECTED INPUT SHAPE, AND NORMALIZED BY SCALING PIXEL VALUES TO THE RANGE [0, 1]. THE PREPROCESSED IMAGE WAS PASSED TO THE TRAINED XCEPTION MODEL FOR PREDICTION. THE MODEL RETURNED A SET OF CLASS PROBABILITIES, AND THE CLASS WITH THE HIGHEST PROBABILITY WAS CHOSEN AS THE PREDICTED LABEL.)
/Pg 127 0 R
/K [3]
